// Adjacent to 0916: the same missing-rigid-filter shape, but with a DRIVER
// predicate joined to the `since` on a variable the ANCHOR binds
// (`input.doc: d`). In the temporal engine this routes the since read through
// the k0-seek join path (`to_join_on_since_key`) instead of the standalone
// read — so it pins the OTHER same-step compensation site, plus the
// GuardRel binding lookup across an `exists` scope boundary (the
// RequestRelation for `context.input.user` sits one binder ABOVE the since).
//
// Same semantics as 0916 otherwise: at the anchor's own timepoint (@0) the
// left is vacuously true over the empty range → PERMIT regardless of the
// correlation; @10 pins the per-user guard streak over the history path;
// @20 is the deny control (dave's intervening event breaks eve's streak).
//
// Interpreter is the oracle (see expected_1.out). Found by differential
// review of the temporal-compiler since compensation paths.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (d: String). (
        Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.doc: d }
        && (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
            since within 1h
            Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.doc: d, input.user: "carol" })
    )
};
